# Windows batch files must keep CRLF line endings. cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only
# batch files, which silently breaks them (the PowerShell call inside never
# runs, or the script dies at the first if-block). Without this rule a clone
# with core.autocrlf=false, or a gateway that normalises on checkout, hands
# the user a broken installer. See scripts/gen_wrappers.py.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
